# Git checks out every authored file in plugin/ with LF line endings, whatever a
# machine's core.autocrlf says (https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes#_eol), so
# a clone of plugin/, such as a host's install from this repository, holds the
# bytes committed on every platform; each vendored folder below keeps upstream's.
plugin/** text eol=lf
# Git keeps each vendored skill folder's bytes as upstream wrote them, so each
# copy matches the blobs its record names. A later line wins, so these come last:
# https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes#_text
.agents/skills/writing-for-agents/** -text
plugin/skills/defuddle/** -text
plugin/skills/json-canvas/** -text
plugin/skills/knap/** -text
plugin/skills/obsidian-bases/** -text
plugin/skills/obsidian-cli/** -text
plugin/skills/obsidian-markdown/** -text
